From d8b9fbb727c2409de1e911725e87ee921c11e84a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Meng Li <Meng.Li@windriver.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Jun 2025 17:13:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drivers: video: nvcsi-t194: fix the failure of creating
 device link

During system boots up, there is below error reported:
t194-nvcsi 13e00000.host1x:nvcsi@15a00000: Failed to create
device link (0x180) with 9-001a.
In tegra234-p3737-camera-imx477-overlay.dts file, there are
endpoints as below
nvcsi@15a00000 {
	......
	imx477_csi_in0: endpoint@0 {
		......
		remote-endpoint = <&imx477_out0>;
	};
	......
}
......
imx477_a@1a {
	......
	imx477_out0: endpoint {
		......
		remote-endpoint = <&imx477_csi_in0>;
	};
}
During the kernel boot process, the nvhost-nvcsi-t194 device
is registered before the nv_imx477 device. This causes
nvhost-nvcsi-t194 to be recognized as a consumer while nv_imx477
is identified as a supplier when parsing the device node for
device linking. However, if nvhost-nvcsi-t194 binds to its driver
before the nv_imx477 device does, the nv_imx477 driver fails to
establish the device link to nvhost-nvcsi-t194. This occurs because
nvhost-nvcsi-t194 is actually the consumer device and has already
been successfully probed beforehand, which violates the device link
policy. To resolve this issue, we ensure that the nv_imx477 device
is probed prior to nvhost-nvcsi-t194 device.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Meng Li <Meng.Li@windriver.com>
---
 drivers/video/tegra/host/nvcsi/nvcsi-t194.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/video/tegra/host/nvcsi/nvcsi-t194.c b/drivers/video/tegra/host/nvcsi/nvcsi-t194.c
index 95dc515..63a4269 100644
--- a/drivers/video/tegra/host/nvcsi/nvcsi-t194.c
+++ b/drivers/video/tegra/host/nvcsi/nvcsi-t194.c
@@ -276,3 +276,4 @@ static struct platform_driver t194_nvcsi_driver = {
 
 module_platform_driver(t194_nvcsi_driver);
 MODULE_LICENSE("GPL");
+MODULE_SOFTDEP("pre: nv_imx477");
-- 
2.34.1

